  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical iron ball of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> is coated with a layer of ice of uniform thickness that melts at a rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;When the thickness of the ice is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the rate at which the thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo></math>in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;of the ice decreases, is :",
